UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Moon represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Distortions and Fluctuating Subconscious Telemetry''—the murky, high-distortion phase where the sovereign consciousness must navigate the twilight realm of instinct, deep psychological shadows, illusion, and unmapped emotional depths. Moving beyond the peaceful, radiant clarity of The Star, The Moon signifies the stage of ''The Path of the Unseen Elements,'' where your usual rational scripts and bright analytical filters fail to illuminate the terrain, forcing you to rely on primal instincts and raw emotional intelligence to detect hidden subcurrents. Visually depicted as a full moon containing a crescent profile shining between two dark, ominous towers, shedding drops of light onto a landscape where a wolf and a domesticated dog howl at the sky while a primitive crayfish emerges from a dark pool to start a long, winding path into the unknown, this archetype embodies the concept of ''The Twilight Threshold''—the realization that true spiritual and mental mastery requires crossing the wild, chaotic wilderness of your subconscious mind without succumbing to paranoia or deceptive projections. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Subconscious Database Defragmentation,'' where repressed fears, ancestral conditioning, and highly volatile dream data rise to the surface, creating a temporary, high-latency distortion in your daily perspective. When The Moon appears, your system is registering an ''Ambiguity-Peak'' status; you are being invited to stop demanding rigid, black-and-white certainty, allow your hidden shadows to step into high visibility, and walk through the mist with quiet, instinctual focus.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When The Moon appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''The Clearance of Delusion, Exposing the Shadows, or the Climax of Paranoia''—a critical tipping point where the fog of self-deception begins to lift, or conversely, your refusal to face the subconscious has triggered an absolute overload of anxiety, confusion, and psychological gridlock. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates ''obsessive over-analysis, reading into every anomaly, or feeding a narrative of hidden betrayal'' with ''being hyper-vigilant and safe,'' even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a critical failure from severe psychological exhaustion. You are essentially ''chasing ghosts in your own network lines,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to ''project its inner terror onto external situations and blame unseen enemies'' over the sober, unglamorous requirement to sit still, turn your gaze inward, and let the emotional storm run its course. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''shrewd, hyper-aware detective who sees through everything,'' while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of disorientation, unremitting panic, or absolute fragmentation, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of ''fighting illusions of your own making,'' and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your current perspective is a trap. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a ''feedback loop of manufactured anxiety and avoidance''; you are obsessively inventing external conspiracies to avoid the quiet cemetery of your own unhealed trauma, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final stabilization of your spirit is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to clear the smoke and stand still, you would be forced to confront the terrifying reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these frantic, fear-amplifying, illusion-chasing scripts, perform a brutal audit of your emotional fabrications, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize pristine, quiet self-honesty over the convenience of a dramatic, chaotic maze. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance anxiety, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and completely unfettered reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 75;
